{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786510220,"nonce":"z+NR75d1n1wyLJfvbNKDJdBQo/U=","target":"cc0fac27ebf7aaaad99b3c1792c90e055ecaf2aa3b8773ff00f177387a88f2c5","message":"Title: `orgLister.Scopes` claims to be the reminder sweep's query and is not: it drops `deleted_at IS NULL`, so every sweep visits deleted tenants forever\n\n**What is wrong.** `orgLister` says in its own doc comment that it is a copy of a query that already exists — `internal/app/adapters.go:844-847`: *\"`notification/repository.ReminderRepository` already publishes exactly this query for its own sweep; this is the same list for the reaper, the group close and the flap score.\"*\n\nIt is not the same query. Five lines below, `internal/app/adapters.go:852`:\n\n```\nconst listOrgIDsSQL = `SELECT id FROM orgs ORDER BY id`\n```\n\nAnd the query it claims to be, `internal/notification/repository/reminders.go:44`:\n\n```\nconst listOrgsSQL = `SELECT id FROM orgs WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY id`\n```\n\nThe neighbour filters soft-deleted tenants. The copy does not, and has no `LIMIT` either. `orgs.deleted_at` is soft-delete only — `db/migrations/00003_identity.sql:28` declares the column and `:43-44` states *\"Soft delete. Expand/contract only -- rows are never removed by a migration.\"* A deleted tenant's row is permanent, so every sweep driven by `orgLister` sweeps it on every tick, forever.\n\n**The demonstration.** `c.orgs` is this lister (`internal/app/container.go:269`), and it drives every global periodic:\n\n- `forEachOrg` (`internal/app/workers.go:149-163`) backs `occurrence.reap`, which issues **two** service calls per tenant per minute — `Reap` at `:177` and `ExpireSnoozes` at `:192` — plus `group.close` (`:207-220`) each minute and `flap.score` every five.\n- `effectiveRetention` (`:295-326`) adds one `GetOrg` per tenant, hourly (`internal/platform/jobs/registry.go:280`).\n- `sweepDrills` (`:371-392`) walks the list again inside `retention.prune`.\n- `Reconciler.FanOut` (`internal/sources/service/reconcile.go:637-657`) walks it on a 30-second tick (`internal/app/workers.go:28,47`).\n- `stats.rollup` walks it every 15 minutes (`internal/stats/worker/rollup.go:56`).\n\nAt 500 tenants: `occurrence.reap` issues 1 000 sequential queries a minute against a 2-minute timeout (`registry.go:202`). The 30-second reconcile tick issues 500 sequential `ListDue` calls, and because `fanOutTenant` enqueues two job requests per due source — `SourceReconcileArgs` and `SilencesSyncArgs`, `internal/sources/service/reconcile.go:671-681` — a tick at the per-tenant ceiling of `FanOutLimit = 200` (`:93`) enqueues up to 200 000 job requests. None of that count decreases when a customer leaves; the deleted tenant contributes its share of every tick indefinitely.\n\nThe per-tenant work is carefully bounded and the tenant list is not. `internal/app/workers.go:140-142`: *\"sweepLimit bounds one tick's work per tenant. A sweep that is not bounded is a sweep that becomes an outage the first time somebody has a bad night.\"* `sweepLimit = 500` caps rows per org; nothing caps orgs.\n\n`internal/notification/service/reminder.go:88-108` reads its list from `ReminderRepository.ListOrgIDs`, so the unacked-reminder sweep is the one that correctly skips deleted tenants. It shares the missing `LIMIT`, not the soft-delete defect.\n\n**Why it matters.** The correct pattern is not a design question to be resolved — it is thirty lines away in another package, and the defective query's own comment asserts it was copied from there. Whatever reasoning made `deleted_at IS NULL` right for the reminder sweep applies unchanged to the reaper, the group close, the flap score, the drill sweep, the retention window and the rollup.\n\n**Where.** `internal/app/adapters.go:852` (the query) and `:844-847` (the comment that misdescribes it), `internal/notification/repository/reminders.go:44` (the correct sibling), `internal/app/container.go:269` (the wiring), `internal/app/workers.go:149-163`, `:295-326`, `:371-392`, `internal/sources/service/reconcile.go:642`, `internal/stats/worker/rollup.go:56` (the consumers), `db/migrations/00003_identity.sql:43-44`.\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** `listOrgIDsSQL` filters `deleted_at IS NULL` and pages rather than returning the whole table, and the fan-outs that walk it enqueue per-tenant jobs instead of looping every tenant inside one handler.","files":null}]}